# .npmignore — belt-and-braces only. The REAL exclusion is the "!dist/delivery"
# negation in package.json's `files` array.
#
# WHY: npm ignores .npmignore entirely when `files` is declared — verified with
# `npm pack --dry-run`, which still listed dist/delivery/*.js until the negation
# was added to `files`. This file is kept so the intent is visible to anyone
# reading the package root, and in case `files` is ever removed.
#
# WHAT IS AT STAKE: dist/delivery/premium.js has premium source COMPILED IN.
# Publishing it would ship closed-source premium code to every free installer —
# the exact leak this architecture exists to prevent.
#
# Verify after ANY packaging change:
#   npm pack --dry-run --ignore-scripts | grep delivery    → must return nothing
dist/delivery/
